{"seq":15,"trial_id":"harness-zero-select-2026-11/zero-full-no-effort-high-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-05T22:03:21.728Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"2c9cd65c86d4d4d5d114a312aee6b0295ed149ae0ae010eaf871287824152bc7","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes:\n\n1. **#PD-4492**, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers checking in at Dock Doors 14–18 at the Eau Claire yard weren't getting text messages with their bay assignments. A fix went in that evening, and Thea confirmed the 04:00 shift on 5 Oct got through the gate without help. The note also says to archive the Eau Claire kiosk logs before the 14 Oct maintenance window.\n2. **#4419**, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners couldn't read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing. Since this note has no date, I can't tell whether it came before or after #PD-4492.\n\nSome things I left out:\n- Moss's two other North notes (the 2025-09-14 pipeline digest and the 2026-03-23 renewal check-in) mention Quarrendon Freight Lines but give no ticket numbers.\n- Tickets #4409 and #4412 and FR-882 in Moss's Central notes are about Marrow accounts, not this one.\n- Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" is about a different company that isn't a Pemberline customer.\n\nI only searched Moss's notes in the shared files you can open. There's no folder of Moss's own personal notes there, so if Moss keeps notes somewhere else, I haven't seen them."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
